{"name":"Hibiscus Punch","hex":"#5c3d45","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hibiscus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Hibiscus, especially Hibiscus syriacus, found in tropical to temperate regions, of some species used for making infusions/tea.","A cocktail made with champagne and cranberry juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hibiscus"},{"term":"punch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hit or strike with one's fist.","A blow from something other than the fist."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike with one's fist.","To herd (cattle) as a cowboy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Punch (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"The term punch refers to a wide assortment of drinks, both alcoholic and non-alcoholic, generally containing fruits or fruit juice. The drink was introduced from the Indian subcontinent to England by employees of the East India Company in the late 17th century. Punch is usually served at parties in large, wide bowls, known as punch bowls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG/330px-Bowle_Steinhude_2009_20090822_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punch_(drink)","wikidata":"Q1121224"},{"title":"Hibiscus","blocks":[{"text":"Hibiscus is a genus of plants in the family Malvaceae native to the tropics and subtropics. The genus is quite large, comprising 319 species. Hibiscus are renowned for their large, showy flowers and those species are commonly known simply as \"hibiscus\", or less widely known as rose mallow. The genus includes both annual and perennial herbaceous plants, as well as woody shrubs and small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca